filename=design_docs/sustainable_fashion_practices_recommendations.md<br>
# Sustainable Fashion Practices Recommendations<br>
<br>
## Upcycling<br>
Upcycling involves transforming old or discarded materials into new products of higher value. This approach reduces waste and conserves resources, while also promoting creativity and innovation in fashion design.<br>
<br>
## Repurposing<br>
Repurposing involves giving new life to existing materials by reusing them in a different context. This approach reduces the need for raw materials, conserves energy, and promotes sustainability in fashion production.<br>
<br>
## Eco-Friendly Materials<br>
Eco-friendly materials are made from sustainable sources, such as organic cotton, recycled polyester, or plant-based fabrics. These materials reduce the environmental impact of fashion production, while also promoting fair labor conditions.<br>
```<br>
